{
  "id": "pretrees",
  "title": "Pretrees",
  "description": "Sets with a betweenness relation that behaves as in a tree: the axioms, intervals, the theorem that every finite pretree is a set of vertices of a finite tree, directions on linear sets, uniqueness of medians, and dense, complete and median pretrees, with an example of a complete dense pretree that is not median, separable pretrees, whose intervals are ordered like the real interval [0,1], a theorem that recognizes dendrites by a pretree structure, flows, directed arcs with their suprema, the completion of a pretree by its flows, the three kinds of flows, the adjacent points of the completion, discrete pretrees as sets of vertices of trees, quotients of pretrees, the dense quotient, the pretree of cut points of a connected space, the map from such a space to the completion of its set of cut points, and the dendrite quotient of a continuum.",
